# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
venv/
__pycache__/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

tmp/

# Scratch from the tools in tools/*.mjs — a headless Chrome profile and the
# host pages they drive. Untracked, and oxlint should not read them either:
# a browser extension's bundled JS is not our code.
tools/.chrome*/
tools/.screens.html
tools/.edu.html
tools/.partners.html
tools/.maven.html
tools/.ortables.html

# PowerPoint's lock file, written beside info.pptx whenever the deck is open.
~$*.pptx

# Video masters. Image masters are committed — they are a megabyte or two and
# they are the source of truth for the WebPs beside them. A video master is
# 25 MB, which is larger than this entire repository's history, and git keeps
# it forever whether or not it is ever needed again. The encoded file that the
# page actually loads IS committed; keep the master wherever the renders live.
src/assets/**/*.vid.mp4

# The MAVEN deck. src/assets/partners/info.pptx is committed at 2.6 MB as the
# provenance record for third-party trademarks and that trade is worth making;
# this one is 159 MB, which is roughly sixty times the whole of this
# repository's history, and git would keep every future revision of it forever.
# Nothing in the build reads it. Keep it wherever the source material lives.
# Remove this line if you decide the provenance is worth the weight.
src/assets/maven/info.pptx

# The MAVEN detail master, which is not a master: tools/maven-art.mjs renders
# it out of Picture11.emf, and the EMF is committed right beside it. Keeping
# 1.6 MB of PNG that one command reproduces exactly is the same trade the rule
# above refuses. Delete the file and re-run the tool.
src/assets/maven/detail.png

*.pdf
*.pptx
*.step
# The D1 assembly CAD. 73 MB of SolidWorks AP214 that git would keep every
# revision of forever, and nothing in the build reads it: tools/d1-frame.mjs
# turns it into the turntable in src/assets/d1/turn/, and those renders are
# committed. Keep the STEP wherever the CAD lives.
src/assets/d1/*.STEP

# Scratch for tools/d1-frame.mjs: the tessellated mesh and the PNG frames it
# renders before they are cropped and encoded. Only the WebPs are committed.
tools/.d1/

# Scratch profile for tools/check-routes.mjs.
tools/.routes/
tools/.mobile/
tools/.shots/
tools/.webkit/

# Scratch for tools/media-review.mjs: contact sheets and a Chrome profile.
tools/.media/

# The two clips supplied 2026-08-18. 26 MB between them, neither publishable
# as it stands — one is live surgery with an identifiable patient, the other
# carries surface-scan slides. tools/media-review.mjs has the full review.
# Nothing in the build reads them, and git would keep them forever. Keep them
# wherever the footage lives; remove these lines when a cleared, web-encoded
# version exists to commit.
src/assets/media/VIDEO-*.mp4
